# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave DATABASE_URL unset to use the embedded PGlite database at .pglite/
# (no server required — used by `npm test` and by `npm run db:seed` out of the box).
#
# PGlite keeps its database in one directory and one process owns it at a time, so stop
# the dev server before `db:reset` or `db:seed`, then start it again.
#
# For a real Postgres 16 locally: `npm run db:up` starts one via Docker, then set:
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://ccn:ccn@localhost:5433/ccn_registry
DATABASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment  (architecture spec § 7)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL is the POOLED connection the running app uses. Include ?sslmode=require.
# A production build with no DATABASE_URL refuses to start rather than silently falling
# back to the embedded database — see lib/env.ts.
#
# DIRECT_URL is the UNPOOLED connection migrations run over. This is not cosmetic:
# migration 0001 contains CREATE TYPE, CREATE FUNCTION and CREATE TRIGGER statements that
# a pooler in transaction mode (Supabase port 6543, Neon's pooler, any pgbouncer) cannot
# execute. Point it at the direct host, usually port 5432.
DIRECT_URL=

# Comma-separated list of operator emails permitted to request a magic link.
# Nobody can sign in if this is empty.
OPERATOR_EMAILS=operator@example.com

# In development the magic link is printed to the server console instead of emailed.
# There is no mail provider wired yet, so on a deployed host the link appears only in the
# function logs. Wiring one is a deployment step, not a code change here.
